    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a favorable slate today, headlined by the explosive matchup potential for **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite score of 83.29. Henderson benefits from a soft matchup against Bello and favorable wind conditions that amplify his power profile; his 8% BvP edge and optimal lineup positioning make him a locked-in core play. **Kyle Tucker** (74.31) and **Andy Pages** (68.56) also represent high-floor assets against Ryne Nelson, as both hitters enjoy beneficial platoon splits and top-of-the-order run-production opportunities. Conversely, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.75) faces a stiff challenge against the elite arm of Chris Sale; while his power remains dangerous, the matchup against such a high-caliber lefty drags his efficiency score down toward our marginal threshold.\n\nThe most difficult personnel decision centered on **Miguel Andujar**, who ultimately failed to crack the starting nine. While his park factors and base projections were respectable, his 35.83 score fell short of our 40.0 floor, largely due to a harsh matchup against the formidable Wheeler and a negative platoon adjustment that rendered him a liability compared to the rest of the lineup. Meanwhile, we continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, whose lingering IL designations leave the bottom of our roster thin. We are also tracking potential lineup fluctuations for **Brayan Rocchio** and **Coby Mayo**; while their projected spots in the order allow them to remain in the lineup, their efficiency scores remain sensitive to potential drop-offs in their batting order placement. Managers should remain alert to official lineup cards, as any late-scratch or order-shuffling for **Dominic Smith** or **Jackson Merrill**\u2014the latter of whom faces a difficult test against Wheeler\u2014could necessitate a last-minute reevaluation of our daily caps.",
